1
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,077
Where the heck am I?

2
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,160
A lake?

3
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,820
What am I doing here?

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,137
I was just…

5
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,720
That's right!

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:24,410
Oh no!

7
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:28,131
If I don't do something, that
vending machine's in trouble!

8
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,137
I was sure I'd die from a fall like that.

9
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:38,220
But I guess I survived.

10
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:40,697
Well, first things first.

11
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:42,540
Wait, huh?

12
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:43,901
What's going on?

13
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:45,060
Why can't I move?

14
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:48,280
Someone help me, please! Hello there! Huh?

15
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,437
Did I hear my own voice just now?

16
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,840
Okay, calm down

17
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,240
Thank you very much!

18
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,140
Yup, that's my voice!

19
00:00:56,420 --> 00:01:00,440
I look forward to serving you
again I recognize this spiel.

20
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:03,174
I've heard those words countless times.

21
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,927
You could even win a reward.

22
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:08,340
I'm a huge fan of any
and all vending machines.

23
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,557
Everyone knows they're my passion.

24
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,346
I'd never mistake that sound.

25
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:15,357
Which means...

26
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,080
For some reason, I've been
turned into a vending machine!

27
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:30,777
So i died and have been
reborn as a vending

28
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:34,357
machine huh as if that could happen no

29
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,057
matter how obsessed i was there's no way

30
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:41,597
i could turn into one whoa this is awesome

31
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:46,677
there's no other way to explain it i am
a vending machine i'm fully stocked with

32
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:51,257
reasonably priced goods and my new
rectangular body is the perfect combination of

33
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:57,417
elegance and functionality hold on a sec
this can't be happening becoming a vending

34
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:02,357
machine is the worst or is it being reborn

35
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,557
as the thing i loved could this be some

36
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:10,677
sort of gift from the divine well there's
no changing what i am now not sure what

37
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:16,197
it says about me or my fandom that i've
just accepted this hello there thank you.

38
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,110
very much.

39
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:19,418
I look forward to serving you again.

40
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:21,460
You could even win a reward.

41
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:23,780
Too bad. You win!

42
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:27,677
Please insert coins.

43
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,617
Are those phrases all I can say?

44
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,237
I wonder what else I can do.

45
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:34,460
You're a vending machine.
Focus. Become it.

46
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:36,437
Surely you can operate yourself.

47
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,800
This is your body.

48
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:38,960
Understand it.

49
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,280
Oh, in my brain!

50
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,537
Wait, I don't have a brain.

51
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:45,502
A bunch of text and numbers
popped up in my mind.

52
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,397
Are these the goods I have for sale?

53
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,951
There are only two types.

54
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,153
You can use your points to
change your current inventory.

55
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,270
Huh? Really?

56
00:02:55,353 --> 00:02:58,500
So I can change what I'm
selling? Points, huh?

57
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,740
That must be what PT stands for.

58
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:03,437
The money you earn is
converted into points.

59
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:07,277
You may spend points to replenish or
make changes to your stocked goods,

60
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,301
as well as acquire new functions.

61
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:10,720
That makes sense.

62
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:13,719
I did some investigating on my own.

63
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:17,637
It seems spending points not only
lets me keep items hot or cold,

64
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:20,177
it also lets me do things
like heat up frozen food?

65
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:23,140
and even add hot water
to cup ramen on demand.

66
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,637
I might as well test
out my other functions

67
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,340
and check out what kind
of items I can sell.

68
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:33,737
Oh, it looks like I have everything I could
buy from the vending machines back home.

69
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:38,055
Let's try spending 10 points to switch
one of my items to cold milk tea.

70
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,497
It worked.

71
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:44,177
Talk about convenient.

72
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:45,757
100 yen is a good price.

73
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,837
It says here.

74
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,897
I can turn 100 yen into one point.

75
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:50,097
All right.

76
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,997
Time to see what else I can do.

77
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,757
After experimenting a little bit more.

78
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,997
I realized one important thing.

79
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:00,297
My new body doesn't run on electricity.

80
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:04,037
Instead it seems I consume
points to keep myself powered on.

81
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:07,437
I use one point an hour.

82
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,957
So I need 24 points a day to function.

83
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:14,977
Which means I have to sell at least
2400 yen worth of product every day.

84
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:17,597
I still have nearly a thousand points.

85
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,397
So I can run for about a month.

86
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:23,117
But I shouldn't waste any points
until I can get a steady income.

87
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,580
Wait.

88
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:28,129
Will I actually get
any customers out here?

89
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,280
Nobody's come by!

90
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,337
All I'm doing is losing points here!

91
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:40,237
If this keeps up, I won't make
enough and I'll run out of juice!

92
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,150
Huh?

93
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:46,370
A frog?

94
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,477
But it's almost as big as a person.

95
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,266
Plus, it's wearing armor
and holding a weapon.

96
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,877
You know, I should probably
be a little more surprised,

97
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:59,160
but turning into a vending machine
kind of one ups this oh hello there

98
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:04,220
uh um hi there

99
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:08,960
hold on stop

100
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:14,117
three damage durability
has been decreased by

101
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:17,797
three what's durability
if your durability is

102
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:20,357
exhausted the vending
machine will break and become

103
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:23,380
unusable so it's like hit
points in a video Okay,

104
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:25,272
how many do I have left?

105
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:26,670
There it is.

106
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,213
These must be my stats.

107
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:31,237
Everything but durability
and toughness is zero.

108
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:34,438
I suppose a vending machine
doesn't need those stats.

109
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:35,820
Wait, magic?

110
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:38,324
Does magic exist in this world?

111
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:42,193
You can spend points in order
to restore your durability.

112
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:43,250
That's good.

113
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:45,060
I still have about 900 points left.

114
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,946
Maybe I can get through this.

115
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,177
Oh crap, this is really bad.

116
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:53,142
I don't want to get hit by that!

117
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:56,997
There has to be some sort of
self-defense function in here somewhere.

118
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:57,910
Let's see.

119
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:01,680
Pour hot water, transaction
fanfare, big winner roulette.

120
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,257
I can't use any of these!

121
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:06,957
Come on, there's got to be something
I can do to get out of this!

122
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,920
Two damage.

123
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:09,997
Durability has been decreased by two.

124
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:10,910
Aw, damn it!

125
00:06:10,993 --> 00:06:12,017
I need help each other!

126
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:14,157
Durability has been decreased by four.

127
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,660
Blessing? What's this?

128
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,437
It's a special power granted by a god.

129
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,657
You may acquire a
blessing without spending

130
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:23,377
any of your points I
don't really understand,

131
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,317
but it's some sort of magic, right?

132
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:29,840
Okay, let's do it Can I even use
swordsmanship or martial arts?

133
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:32,057
Last time I checked I don't
have any arms or legs.

134
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,905
There has to be something else

135
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:38,297
Barrier deploys an invisible
barrier around you.

136
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,877
You can designate what
objects are allowed through.

137
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,380
Yeah, I picked that one

138
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,440
You could even win a reward!

139
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:52,870
Yeah!

140
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,735
Behold the invincible vending machine!

141
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,178
I look forward to serving you again.

142
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:00,490
Huh?

143
00:07:00,573 --> 00:07:01,403
Wait a second.

144
00:07:01,486 --> 00:07:04,166
How come I'm losing so
many points so quickly?

145
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:05,370
Huh?

146
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,120
Give it up, guys!

147
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:10,399
All you're doing is wasting
your time and my points!

148
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:15,830
Whew!

149
00:07:15,913 --> 00:07:16,743
I made it!

150
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,829
I might as well get my
durability back now.

151
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,660
There. Good as new.

152
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:26,360
I've got 311 points left.

153
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:28,860
I can still last over 10 days.

154
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:32,657
But unless somebody buys something, my
points will dry up and I'll run out of power.

155
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:34,337
But what happens after that?

156
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:35,300
Will I die?

157
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,017
What a tragically short life.

158
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:40,740
Or, I suppose, a short operating
time? Somebody! Anybody!

159
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:42,540
Please help me!

160
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:49,897
It would have been pretty cool to
sell at least one thing before dying.

161
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:52,720
There's no use trying to hide from me!

162
00:08:01,340 --> 00:08:02,170
What the?

163
00:08:02,253 --> 00:08:04,573
I could have sworn they were around here

164
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,837
Thank goodness, I'm starving.

165
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:11,240
I'm so hungry I can't
muster up any strength!

166
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,957
Why does this kind of
thing always happen to me?

167
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:17,437
I even dropped my bag
with all my food in it!

168
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:18,500
It's my fault!

169
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,957
I should have listened!

170
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,216
My parents were right, I'm
not cut out to be a hunter!

171
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,831
What's she talking about?

172
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:27,548
I have to defeat frog
fiends for their meat.

173
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:28,630
For some reason,

174
00:08:28,713 --> 00:08:32,537
my attacks don't hit when I'm by
myself and I just want to take a nap!

175
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:35,561
Things will be better if
I at least add some food.

176
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,380
Wait, what's that?

177
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:41,080
So weird.

178
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:44,377
Looks like some kind of stone
monument, but too Middle.

179
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:46,460
The shape is really peculiar, too.

180
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:49,155
And are those drinks behind the glass?

181
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,877
There's a bunch of writing,
but I can't read it.

182
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,790
Hello, man!

183
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,337
Wait, what was that voice?

184
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,317
Where'd it come from?

185
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:58,160
Please insert coins. The box.

186
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,460
How is it talking?

187
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:01,800
Also, coins? It wants money?

188
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:03,611
Would a copper coin work?

189
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:05,999
Maybe it has to be at least silver.

190
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,614
What if it needs gold?

191
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,120
As if I even had that on me.

192
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:13,137
It said something about
inserting the coins.

193
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:16,867
I guess it can't hurt to put in
a copper and see what happens.

194
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:21,642
Looks like a copper coin
wasn't enough after all.

195
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:24,062
That is an unsupported currency.

196
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:27,057
If you acquire the coin conversion
function, you can accept it.

197
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:27,970
What?

198
00:09:28,053 --> 00:09:28,883
For real?

199
00:09:28,966 --> 00:09:29,796
Hold on just one second.

200
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:30,760
Oh, there it is.

201
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,273
I can swing 100 points.

202
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:37,037
I didn't increase the prices, but
the numbers went up all the same.

203
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:37,950
Huh?

204
00:09:38,033 --> 00:09:38,957
Why did the number change?

205
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:39,940
A thousand owa?

206
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,960
Aw, but that's a whole silver coin.

207
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:46,121
So this world's unit of
currency is called an owa.

208
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:48,987
It's expensive, but I
need food for my belly.

209
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,400
I'm about to beg!

210
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,520
It lit up.

211
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:59,414
Ooh, does it want me to push something?

212
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:00,690
Hmm...

213
00:10:00,773 --> 00:10:02,634
Wow, there's a picture of soup on here!

214
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:04,580
Huh? What was that?

215
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:05,818
Something came out!

216
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:10,517
It's not gonna chomp down if
I reach my hand in, right?

217
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:11,718
I wouldn't do that!

218
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,157
So hurry up and take it!

219
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:15,769
I highly recommend this
brand of corn soup!

220
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,820
Oh, it's so warm!

221
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:24,040
Uh, do I twist the top to open it?

222
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,230
Oh!

223
00:10:26,313 --> 00:10:27,260
It smells good!

224
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:35,157
Wow, what is this?

225
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,080
It's so tasty!

226
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:37,477
I wouldn't want Mrs.

227
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:40,977
to hear this, but it's way better
than the food I had in town!

228
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,760
Why do I feel so happy?

229
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:47,592
Helping someone out gives me a sense
of satisfaction I haven't felt before.

230
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:51,020
Aw, man, I drank everything already.

231
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,527
I bet the other stuff
in there is tasty, too.

232
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:59,177
The clear-looking ones are probably water,
And I already know what that tastes like,

233
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:01,789
so I'll try out the
light brown drink next.

234
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:05,740
It seems she took a liking
to the milk tea as well.

235
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:10,492
Afterwards, she bought three more corn
soups, along with a bottle of water.

236
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:15,660
I earned six silver coins and 30
coppers for a total of 6,300 owa,

237
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,420
which means I got back 63 points!

238
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:26,297
A full stomach must have broken
the tension she was holding.

239
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:29,204
As soon as she finished
eating, she fell asleep.

240
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:32,956
She's a bit of an odd one,
but she's my best customer.

241
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:33,950
Don't worry.

242
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:36,119
I'll keep you safe with my barrier.

243
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:39,200
The trash cleans itself up!

244
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:43,819
I've got to be the most advanced
vending machine in this other world!

245
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:51,140
Looks like I fell asleep.

246
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:54,777
Well, it's a good thing
no monsters showed up.

247
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:57,100
I ended up spending a whole bunch.

248
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,077
But I'm feeling a lot better now.

249
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,780
And it's all thanks to you.

250
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,156
Thank you very much.

251
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:03,740
Uh, yes.

252
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:05,060
Um, thank you.

253
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,620
That's right.

254
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,540
I forgot that you can talk.

255
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:12,697
Or maybe...

256
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:15,192
Are you only able to say certain phrases?

257
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:19,537
I actually know someone who's inventing
tools that have magical power inside them.

258
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:21,796
I wonder if you're something similar.

259
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:25,817
If you can understand what I'm saying,
then I'd like it if you said something.

260
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:26,730
Anything.

261
00:12:26,813 --> 00:12:27,643
Hello there.

262
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,097
Yes, I knew it.

263
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,757
I bet Hulemy would be
interested in meeting you.

264
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,980
Oh, I haven't told you my name yet.

265
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,240
You can call me Lamas.

266
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:38,830
Lamas, huh?

267
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,574
Has a nice ring to it.

268
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:41,840
I got it.

269
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:42,957
How's this sound?

270
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:45,697
Whenever you want to say yes,
you can just say hello there,

271
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:47,957
and we'll use a different
phrase to mean no.

272
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:48,870
Too bad.

273
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:52,497
Okay, is that what you
want to use for know then?

274
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:54,860
Hello there. Yes, huh? Perfect.

275
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,077
Let's see.

276
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,457
Can you tell me your name?

277
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,370
Too bad.

278
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:00,930
That's okay.

279
00:13:01,013 --> 00:13:03,220
So what are you doing out here all alone?

280
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:06,500
Are you on some sort of
important quest? Too bad.

281
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,821
I hope I'm not being too forward.

282
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:11,900
Are you lonely by yourself? Hello there.

283
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,560
I thought that was the case.

284
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:16,900
For some reason you looked lonely.

285
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:20,817
Would it be okay with you if
I moved you somewhere else?

286
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:21,730
Hello there!

287
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,722
That's awesome!

288
00:13:23,180 --> 00:13:26,757
I was thinking about bringing you
back and showing you to Hewla me.

289
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:29,497
I bet the two of you would
hit it off right away.

290
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,410
Hello there!

291
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:32,340
You're cool with it? Great!

292
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:33,994
Give me just a second.

293
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:36,420
Up we go!

294
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,080
Are you for real?

295
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:40,554
I have to weigh at least 500 kilograms!

296
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,079
Whoa, you're heavier than you look.

297
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:54,880
Thank you for saving me!

298
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:01,957
Apparently, Lamas has a blessing
called the blessing of might.

299
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:05,275
I suppose that explains why
she's so incredibly strong.

300
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:09,671
I'm just going to take a short break here.

301
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:11,760
I'm starting to get hungry.

302
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:15,177
I wonder if I can buy more
of that tasty yellow soup.

303
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:18,025
The thing is, corn soup
isn't all that filling.

304
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:20,067
Oh, what else could I stock?

305
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,800
Oh, how about that?

306
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,030
Huh?

307
00:14:26,113 --> 00:14:26,959
That surprised me.

308
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,600
You are glowing.

309
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,360
Did you change your items?

310
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:32,740
What is that?

311
00:14:32,980 --> 00:14:34,000
Could it be food?

312
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:34,970
Hello there!

313
00:14:35,053 --> 00:14:36,360
I thought it might be!

314
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,120
It's the same price.

315
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:39,720
Maybe I'll buy some.

316
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,560
Oh, what a weird texture!

317
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:53,115
The only thing I can really taste is
salt, but I can't stop eating them!

318
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,740
Oh, no, no, no! No,

319
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,537
I'm gonna burn through the
rest of my money at this rate,

320
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:59,220
but I can't control myself!

321
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:04,120
Thanks to that, I'm back up to 320 points!

322
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:07,993
Next, I want to try to adjust
the price of mineral water.

323
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:13,917
It'd be great if I could offer it for
less, but my life kind of depends on it.

324
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:18,980
We should reach the entrance of this
stratum soon stratum after that.

325
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:21,355
We'll take a break in a nearby village

326
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,300
Wait Lamas, you're all right.

327
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:34,637
Karios and Gorth boy am I
glad to see you guys whoo!

328
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:38,180
We were worried after your
group came back all but dead.

329
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:39,230
Thank goodness.

330
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:40,143
You're okay.

331
00:15:40,226 --> 00:15:43,160
Sorry about that By the
way, what's this thing?

332
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:47,057
It's a magic tool with its own consciousness
that I found near the lakeside.

333
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:50,077
Whenever you put money in,
it gives you a tasty item.

334
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:50,990
Really?

335
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:53,097
I've never heard of magic tools being

336
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:56,062
discovered in the Clear
Flow Lake stratum before.

337
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,957
Should I have not brought it out?

338
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,160
It's not a problem.

339
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,117
You know how things are in the dungeon.

340
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:05,788
Whatever you find lying around
in a stratum is yours to keep.

341
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,550
Dungeon?

342
00:16:09,633 --> 00:16:11,477
I don't really understand
what they're talking about.

343
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:15,972
They make it sound like we're in some
kind of labyrinth, but there's a sky.

344
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:19,560
Hey, do you think we could
try out your magic item?

345
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,137
Sure, let me ask it.

346
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:23,640
Do you mind? Hello?

347
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:25,940
Whoa, it talked!

348
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:29,417
Right, you said it had a consciousness.

349
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:30,917
This'd fetch a high price.

350
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,220
He's not for sale.

351
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:35,897
I'm going to bring him back with me
so Hulemy can take a look at him.

352
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,560
That engineer who's a magic item fanatic.

353
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,517
A silver coin, huh?

354
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,780
Pretty pricey.

355
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:46,760
But I'll have one of these.

356
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:48,380
Please insert coins.

357
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:52,520
Well, I'll be.

358
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,077
This stuff's delicious.

359
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:55,000
So's this one.

360
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:57,637
I wonder what this
fried-looking thing tastes like.

361
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,550
Let me try.

362
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:02,460
In the end, they bought at
least one of every item I had.

363
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:06,617
Being able to drink both hot and
cold things on demand is great.

364
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:08,517
We aren't allowed to leave our posts.

365
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,617
So could you bring it by now and again?

366
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:11,530
Sure.

367
00:17:11,613 --> 00:17:14,440
And with that, I tripled my customer base.

368
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,500
Wait a sec.

369
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:32,744
I've had enough of your crying.

370
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:34,217
You're wasting our time here.

371
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,947
You're just making things
worse for yourself.

372
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,157
What the hell do you think you're doing?

373
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:41,537
I should ask you the same,

374
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:43,037
because it looks like a bunch of nasty

375
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:45,477
-looking thugs are ganging
up on a helpless girl.

376
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:48,137
Bet you think you're some
kind of hero, don't you?

377
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,737
This will teach you to butt in.

378
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:52,408
You got no one but
yourself to blame, Missy!

379
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:01,417
We'll let you off easy,
but next time you're done.

380
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,618
I look forward to serving you again.

381
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:05,780
Not again.

382
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,293
None of my hits landed.

383
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:09,737
They didn't hurt you, did they?

384
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:11,400
Are you all right? Yes.

385
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:12,720
All thanks to you.

386
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,660
Oh, missus! I'm home!

387
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:21,937
Lamas, you made it back.

388
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:23,680
I was so worried for you.

389
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:25,140
I'm sorry, missus.

390
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:28,660
Oh, Miss, I missed you!

391
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,460
You're alive?

392
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:32,917
I'm not dreaming, am I?

393
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,830
You're not.

394
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:35,273
It's really me, Munami.

395
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:38,080
Oh, I was afraid I'd never see you again.

396
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:41,300
Oh, sorry.

397
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:47,221
When I asked the returning hunters, they
said they ran off and left you by yourself.

398
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:50,957
As revenge, I told everyone
around town what they did.

399
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:53,275
They won't be able to find work again.

400
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:58,937
Anyway what's that uh ah I found it by the

401
00:18:59,020 --> 00:19:01,660
lake you brought back
another weird artifact

402
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:05,037
This one's different
he's surprisingly useful

403
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:07,532
and he helped me out when I was in a bind

404
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:14,377
So you're going back to the
surface to show it to Hulemy

405
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:18,557
do you have enough for the
transfer circle uh can I

406
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:24,317
borrow some money a transfer
circle huh apparently that's

407
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:27,577
a thing in this world also
llamas's lack of funds is kind

408
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:32,637
of my fault whoops sorry
about you you'll just have to

409
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:36,237
work at our end to earn your
fare how about this why don't

410
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:39,097
we keep the box you found
outside it can sell its wares

411
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:43,920
and attract customers hello
there it really can speak

412
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:45,990
Good.

413
00:19:46,073 --> 00:19:47,293
It'll drum up business.

414
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:52,040
And so, I found myself a new
home right in front of the inn.

415
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:53,777
There's a sky,

416
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:58,960
but I soon learned that this was actually
a dungeon stratum called Clear Flow Lake.

417
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:02,057
I quickly gained popularity since my goods

418
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,611
were unlike anything they had seen before.

419
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:09,666
Then, when night fell, Llamas would carry
me over to a safe place near the gate.

420
00:20:10,580 --> 00:20:14,580
I'm feeling kind of thirsty, but
I'm getting tired of this election.

421
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:19,417
Well, that's because you're buying
at least five of them every night!

422
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,377
I suppose I could switch up my stock.

423
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:23,220
What's my current status?

424
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:28,377
After all the business
I've been getting recently,

425
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:31,680
looks like I've saved up
over 3,000 points Great!

426
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:33,260
What should I add?

427
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:39,064
One should always keep the customer's needs
in mind first I've got just the thing!

428
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,687
All the items are different!

429
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:48,293
Whoa, this one costs three silver coins.

430
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:50,537
But at that price, it has to be good.

431
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:51,620
I gotta try it.

432
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,220
How hot?

433
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:57,048
How do you open this thing?

434
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:58,731
Look, are those pictures?

435
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:00,568
Those must be instructions.

436
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:04,617
This item became famous in a
certain electric town back home.

437
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:09,457
So the manufacturer added meticulous
instructions so even tourists could enjoy it.

438
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:10,640
Oh, it worked.

439
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,400
Sure smells good.

440
00:21:16,860 --> 00:21:17,690
What?

441
00:21:17,773 --> 00:21:18,700
This is amazing.

442
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:20,587
It might be my new favorite.

443
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,697
What ingredients did they use in this?

444
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:25,900
The flavor in it is so
complex, yet incredibly light.

445
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,997
Damn, I want alcohol now.

446
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,740
Scooch over a bit. Hold on.

447
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:31,177
I was going to buy something else.

448
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:32,337
They're totally hooked.

449
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:33,250
Hurry up, then.

450
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:35,214
I got plenty more where that came from.

451
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:39,377
My goods only got more popular.

452
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:42,097
Words soon got around
about the canned Odin?

453
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:44,277
Which caused a bit of an
uproar in the village!

454
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:48,478
I think the weather getting colder
lately might have helped sales too.

455
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:53,501
What's more, the sports drink I
added to my stock was also selling.

456
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:56,257
I don't sell canned Odin during the day.

457
00:21:56,340 --> 00:21:58,497
That's when the restaurant
does most of its business.

458
00:21:58,580 --> 00:22:00,057
And I don't want to step on any toes.

459
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:02,840
Instead, I help attract guests.

460
00:22:07,180 --> 00:22:10,217
Isn't this the girl Llamas saved
in the alley the other day?

461
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:12,120
Excuse me! Hello there!

462
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:16,344
I wanted to talk first so I'd have
the advantage in negotiations!

463
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:20,260
Stop that!

464
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:24,360
What was that about?

465
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:30,006
When the sun starts to set, Llamas
carries me over to the gate.

466
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:33,037
She said moving me around
like before was inconvenient,

467
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:36,649
so she bought a wooden frame
that she could put on her back.

468
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:40,900
I'm about to burst.

469
00:22:41,140 --> 00:22:42,611
I'll be heading back now.

470
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:48,057
A guest came by the inn today and
told me tons of interesting stories.

471
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:48,970
Hello there.

472
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,727
How are things on your side?

473
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:52,567
You could even win a reward.

474
00:22:52,780 --> 00:22:54,200
Did you have fun today?

475
00:22:56,040 --> 00:22:59,240
I hope someday you and I can
have a real conversation.

476
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:04,557
That's one of the reasons I want to hurry
and save up so we can go see Hulemy.

477
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:06,040
Thank you very much.

478
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,020
You don't have to thank me.

479
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:09,280
Don't forget it.

480
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:11,538
You were the one who saved me, Boxo.

481
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,190
Boxo?

482
00:23:13,273 --> 00:23:15,845
It feels kind of weird
to keep calling you you.

483
00:23:16,220 --> 00:23:18,080
What do you think? You win!

484
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:19,660
Glad you like it.

485
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,840
Here's to the future, Boxo.

486
00:23:23,260 --> 00:23:27,672
Waking up as a vending machine in
another world is as ridiculous as can be.

487
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,180
But for some reason,

488
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:33,224
I'm starting to think this wouldn't
be such a bad life after all.

489
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,760
Thank you very much!

490
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,118
I look forward to serving you again!
